Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.04,0:00:01.88,Default,,0,0,0,,While I repot this seedling,\Nhere's
Dialogue: 0,0:00:01.88,0:00:04.08,Default,,0,0,0,,why Pandora's famous box was never
Dialogue: 0,0:00:04.08,0:00:05.12,Default,,0,0,0,,actually a box.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:06.60,0:00:08.48,Default,,0,0,0,,The clue is in Hesiod's works
Dialogue: 0,0:00:08.48,0:00:09.26,Default,,0,0,0,,and days.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:09.84,0:00:11.68,Default,,0,0,0,,Prometheus steals fire and gives\Nit
Dialogue: 0,0:00:11.68,0:00:12.26,Default,,0,0,0,,to humanity.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:13.20,0:00:15.28,Default,,0,0,0,,Zeus answers by ordering Pandora\Nto
Dialogue: 0,0:00:15.28,0:00:15.84,Default,,0,0,0,,be created.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:16.58,0:00:18.16,Default,,0,0,0,,The Olympian gods furnish her with
Dialogue: 0,0:00:18.16,0:00:18.46,Default,,0,0,0,,gifts.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:19.82,0:00:21.86,Default,,0,0,0,,Then Zeus sends Pandora to\NPrometheus's
Dialogue: 0,0:00:21.86,0:00:23.30,Default,,0,0,0,,brother, Epimetheus.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:24.78,0:00:27.36,Default,,0,0,0,,Prometheus had already warned\NEpimetheus not
Dialogue: 0,0:00:27.36,0:00:28.64,Default,,0,0,0,,to trust gifts from Zeus.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:30.28,0:00:32.56,Default,,0,0,0,,Epimetheus accepts Pandora anyway.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:32.56,0:00:34.84,Default,,0,0,0,,Beside her stands the object,\Nlater
Dialogue: 0,0:00:34.84,0:00:35.84,Default,,0,0,0,,remembered as a box.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:36.94,0:00:38.90,Default,,0,0,0,,But Hesiod's vessel is a pythos.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:38.90,0:00:40.90,Default,,0,0,0,,A pythos is a large storage
Dialogue: 0,0:00:40.90,0:00:41.96,Default,,0,0,0,,jar, not a chest.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:43.14,0:00:44.70,Default,,0,0,0,,Pandora opens the jar.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:44.70,0:00:46.60,Default,,0,0,0,,Hardships pour out into human\Nlife.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:46.60,0:00:48.92,Default,,0,0,0,,She closes the lid, but not
Dialogue: 0,0:00:48.92,0:00:50.24,Default,,0,0,0,,before they are gone.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:50.24,0:00:52.10,Default,,0,0,0,,One thing remains inside.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:52.10,0:00:53.22,Default,,0,0,0,,Elpis.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:53.22,0:00:56.22,Default,,0,0,0,,Elpis is often translated as hope.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:56.60,0:00:58.22,Default,,0,0,0,,What that remaining hope means is
Dialogue: 0,0:00:58.22,0:00:58.96,Default,,0,0,0,,still debated.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:59.68,0:01:02.00,Default,,0,0,0,,That ambiguity changes the story's\Nending.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:03.40,0:01:05.06,Default,,0,0,0,,Pandora is not simply a villain.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:05.80,0:01:07.36,Default,,0,0,0,,She is part of Zeus' punishment
Dialogue: 0,0:01:07.36,0:01:09.30,Default,,0,0,0,,after Prometheus steals fire.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:10.18,0:01:12.04,Default,,0,0,0,,The famous box belongs to later
Dialogue: 0,0:01:12.04,0:01:12.48,Default,,0,0,0,,tradition.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:13.72,0:01:15.24,Default,,0,0,0,,The older story leaves us with
Dialogue: 0,0:01:15.24,0:01:17.54,Default,,0,0,0,,a jar and an unresolved hope.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:18.58,0:01:20.00,Default,,0,0,0,,The famous box began as a
Dialogue: 0,0:01:20.00,0:01:21.90,Default,,0,0,0,,jar and its final mystery stayed
Dialogue: 0,0:01:21.90,0:01:22.26,Default,,0,0,0,,sealed.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:23.70,0:01:26.06,Default,,0,0,0,,Like and subscribe to Grow More
Dialogue: 0,0:01:26.06,0:01:26.56,Default,,0,0,0,,Questions
